## 1. Security Review Triggers & Read-Only Boundary (`SR1`, `SR13`, `SR14`)

### 1.1 Mandatory Review Triggers (`SR1`)

Run a security review whenever a diff touches any of the following:
- [ ] Authentication, session lifecycle, token/ticket issuance or verification
- [ ] Authorization guards, role/permission definitions, or environment-specific access rules
- [ ] Data-scope isolation (`{{scope_list}}`) in database queries, cache keys, background jobs, exports, or realtime channels
- [ ] Secrets, credentials, encryption keys, or personal/regulated data (PII)
- [ ] File uploads/downloads, archive extraction, user-supplied URLs, webhooks, or external redirects
- [ ] New or upgraded third-party dependencies in lockfiles
- [ ] {{workspace_triggers}}

**Deep review areas** (trace callers/callees one level further and require explicit test evidence for every matrix cell): {{deep_areas}}.

### 1.2 Execution Mode & Non-Destructive Boundary (`SR1`, `SR13`, `SR14`)

- **Mode**: {{mode_description}}
- **Fixed revision (`SR1`)**: Audit the exact revision specified in the handoff (`{{revision_notation}}`); never modify application code or tests during the review.
- **No live exploitation (`SR13`)**: Never run exploit payloads against shared (`develop`, `staging`) or `production` environments, and never paste live secrets or real PII into notes or reports. Verify exclusively via read-only code tracing and local/disposable test runs (`{{local_stack}}`).

### 1.3 Deterministic Audit Coverage Ledger (`SR1`)

Before hunting for vulnerabilities, list every changed or reachable security-relevant unit (route, RPC handler, repository query, background job, webhook, client view) in the **Coverage Ledger**. No security review may sign off as `APPROVED` while any unit remains `UNCOVERED`:

| Unit ID | File & Symbol / Entrypoint | Trust Boundary Crossed | Applicable Checks (`SR3`–`SR10`) | Audit Status (`COVERED` / `UNCOVERED`) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `U-01` | `{{path}}` (`{{operation}}`) | `Client → API → DB` | `SR3`, `SR4`, `SR5` | `COVERED` / `UNCOVERED` |

