## 2. Per-Change Threat Model (`STRIDE-lite`, `SR2`)

Write a concise 5–10 line threat model for the change before inspecting individual lines:

```text
Change:        <one-line summary of the diff @ revision>
Assets:        <from: {{assets}}>
Actors:        <from: {{actors}}>
Entry points:  <routes, RPCs, CLI commands, jobs, webhooks, or UI actions touched>
Boundaries:    <client→API, API→DB, API→{{providers}}, tenant→tenant, env→env>
STRIDE Risks:
  - S (Spoofing):            <can caller forge identity/tenant/ticket, or "n/a">
  - T (Tampering):           <can caller mutate unowned fields/records or bypass state guards, or "n/a">
  - R (Repudiation):         <are sensitive mutations audit-logged with actor + tenant + trace_id, or "n/a">
  - I (Information Leak):    <can responses, errors, logs, caches, or streams leak cross-scope data, or "n/a">
  - D (Denial of Service):   <can unbounded input/pagination/queues/uploads exhaust resources, or "n/a">
  - E (Elevation of Priv):   <can a lower role invoke a higher role's operation, or "n/a">
```

