## 3. Authorization Matrix & Data-Scope Isolation (`SR3`, `SR4`)

### 3.1 Authorization Matrix (`Role × Environment × Action × Object`, `SR3`)

For every added or modified operation, fill out the authorization matrix using the workspace's confirmed roles ({{roles}}) and scopes ({{scope_list}}):

| Operation / Endpoint | Role | Environment ({{environments}}) | Target Object Scope | Expected Outcome | Verification Evidence (Test or `file:line`) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `{{operation}}` | `{{role}}` | `{{env}}` | Own `{{scope_list}}` | Allow (`200`/`201`) | `{{test_or_path}}` |
| `{{operation}}` | `{{role}}` | `{{env}}` | Other `{{scope_list}}` (Anti-IDOR) | Deny (`404` or `403`) | `{{test_or_path}}` |
| `{{operation}}` | Unprivileged / Anonymous | `{{env}}` | Any | Deny (`401` or `403`) | `{{test_or_path}}` |

- Any matrix cell lacking a verifying test or traced server-side guard is recorded as a **`PLAUSIBLE BLOCKER`** (or **`CONFIRMED BLOCKER`** when the guard is provably absent). Client/UI hiding never counts as authorization evidence.

### 3.2 Data-Scope Isolation Checklist (`SR4`)

Verify every changed data path carries the authenticated principal's scope:

| Data Path | Required Scope Binding (`{{scope_list}}`) | Enforced At (`file:line`) | Status (`PASS` / `FAIL`) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Database read/write/replay queries | Bound from verified auth context in `WHERE` clause | `<path:line>` | `PASS` / `FAIL` |
| Cache keys & pub/sub channels | Keyed by `(tenant_id, resource_id)` | `<path:line>` | `PASS` / `FAIL` |
| Background jobs & exports | Job payload validates scope ownership before execution | `<path:line>` | `PASS` / `FAIL` |

